# Build output and downloaded dependencies.
#
# Makina asks agents to build and verify their work, then commits the whole
# task worktree. Anything a build writes that is not ignored here is committed
# with the task and rejected as outside its authored footprint - so these rules
# are what keep the first task that compiles anything from failing the run.
#
# Every directory below is where a prepared input or a bounded output lives:
# the pinned Bun tooling, the locked dependency cache, the supplied sibling
# bytes, the installed modules, and the per-run work directory. Each is
# prepared once by a named command and verified offline by the gate; none of
# it is source. Add your own; nothing below is removed by Makina.

# The pinned Bun tooling, installed by scripts/prepare_tooling.
/.tooling/

# The locked dependency cache, populated by scripts/prepare_locked_dependency_cache.
/.dependency-cache/

# The supplied sibling inputs: each side's released or candidate bytes, placed
# by their holder, never built, fetched, or cached here.
/.supplied/

# The installed modules the compiler and the type definitions need.
/node_modules/

# The per-run work directory: bounded capture files, the scratch home, and the
# run report, all written by one run and gone when the run is.
/.runs/

# OS noise
.DS_Store